WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.057
Requirements work establishes what problem the
system must solve and whose concerns matter.

00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:12.647
Gather needs, examine conflicts and feasibility,
then validate the specification with stakeholders.

00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:15.642
Ask why a technology or deadline is required.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:22.165
Clear boundaries and explicit priorities give
architectural decisions a defensible starting point.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.407
A useful specification connects real needs to
observable acceptance conditions.

00:00:27.407 --> 00:00:31.295
Review wording for ambiguity, consistency and
traceability.

00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:35.843
Examples such as character limits reveal missing
boundary conditions.

00:00:35.843 --> 00:00:42.170
When a requirement changes, follow its links into
design, implementation and tests so the update

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:47.575
remains coherent rather than producing a locally
correct but incompatible feature.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.137
Separate behavior, quality and other constraints,
then assign priorities explicitly.

00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:58.212
Quality requirements often cross component
boundaries and shape architecture.

00:00:58.212 --> 00:01:03.090
Replace words such as fast or secure with scenarios
and observable checks.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:09.022
Functional and quality requirements can both be
mandatory, and both need clear evidence of

00:01:09.022 --> 00:01:09.879
satisfaction.
